S10.2D-R8.3 source-backup verification diagnosis

During the backup gate, both Git bundles and their SHA-256 index were created
successfully. The first two verification invocations lacked a usable repository
context: one omitted the repository, and one ran across the root/chatops
ownership boundary. Neither invocation changed a repository or a bundle.

The bounded correction used each canonical repository with an explicit
safe-directory context while retaining the root-only backup directory. Both
bundles then passed `git bundle verify`; the checksum index passed; the backup
directory is root:root mode 2700 and its files are mode 0600.

No retry altered runtime, database, services, evidence, or source content.
